----
glow
----

glow reads its standard input. When run non-interactively with stdin attached
to an open pipe that never produces data - for example over `ssh host 'glow
file.md'` - it will block waiting for input instead of rendering the given
file. Close stdin explicitly in that case:

```
ssh host 'glow -w 78 file.md < /dev/null'
```

This is upstream behaviour, not specific to this package.
